// The popups area's part registry (#438 S3c): the dialogs, alerts and toasts drawn from src/lib/Nexus/pattern and the alert prompt components.
// Which parts a pack must never style, which it may style only within layout bounds, and which are free. The constants below the named list are
// generated by the census in popupsCriticalClosure.test.ts, which prints the list to paste here when it differs.
// QuitPill (`quit-pill`, `quit-pill-region`) is a plain-toast-like warning: it holds a control, so it is reach, not safe.
// The overlay vocabulary: `modal-*` (backdrop root `modal-<id>`, frame, header, title, body, controls, action, field, footer, close, row, text), `memory-progress*`
// and `save-status-*`. A critical subtree never uses `modal-*`, because a name under a critical root is critical everywhere; the save-problem buttons
// of SavePopupIcon are critical roots named `save-status-alert`.
import { lintPack, type LintResult, type RegistryInput } from '../engine'

